{"step_index":1160,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:30:43Z","thinking":"Examining the data, there are several entries, seemingly company names. It's necessary to understand the context of these entries to determine their significance. Further analysis is needed to identify any patterns or relationships between the provided data points, particularly in the numbered rows.\n\n\nAnalyzing the provided data, a distinction emerges between potential retail locations (bookstores, toy stores, etc.) and established companies with associated revenue figures. The list requires grouping into distinct categories for effective comparison. The revenue data from the second set of entries offers a basis for identifying potential businesses of interest.\n\n\nAnalyzing each row, I need to check if the company information, specifically the revenue and employee count, is present in the master CSV. The user's instruction suggests prioritizing data from \"쿠키딜\" and \"머니핀\", while cross-referencing against the spreadsheet data and searching for address using Bizno. After verifying the data in the existing CSV file, I'll attempt to add any missing entries using information from the user-provided data. Address and phone numbers, if missing, will be searched using other web resources.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction parseCSV(content) {\n  const rows = [];\n  let currentRow = [];\n  let currentField = '';\n  let inQuotes = false;\n  for (let i = 0; i < content.length; i++) {\n    const char = content[i];\n    const nextChar = content[i + 1];\n    if (char === '\"') {\n      if (inQuotes && nextChar === '\"') {\n        currentField += '\"';\n        i++;\n      } else {\n        inQuotes = !inQuotes;\n      }\n    } else if (char === ',' && !inQuotes) {\n      currentRow.push(currentField);\n      currentField = '';\n    } else if ((char === '\\r' || char === '\\n') && !inQuotes) {\n      if (char === '\\r' && nextChar === '\\n') i++;\n      currentRow.push(currentField);\n      if (currentRow.some(f => f.trim() !== '')) rows.push(currentRow);\n      currentRow = [];\n      currentField = '';\n    } else {\n      currentField += char;\n    }\n  }\n  if (currentField !== '' || currentRow.length > 0) {\n    currentRow.push(currentField);\n    if (currentRow.some(f => f.trim() !== '')) rows.push(currentRow);\n  }\n  return rows;\n}\n\nconst csvPath = 'C:/Users/lg/Desktop/Today/(안상숙)(STI)_(모집단현행화)_부산정보산업진흥원_2026_부산_CT산업_실태조사_260910_크레탑_배현명.csv';\nconst content = fs.readFileSync(csvPath, 'utf8');\nconst clean = content.charCodeAt(0) === 0xFEFF ? content.slice(1) : content;\nconst rows = parseCSV(clean);\n\nconsole.log(`Master CSV total rows: ${rows.length}`);\n\n// Check specific key rows\nconst checkRowNums = [703, 639, 649, 1542, 1567, 1630, 1645, 1786, 1789, 1804, 1812, 1815, 1816, 2140, 2141, 2143, 2216, 2223, 2232, 2240, 2243, 2247, 2260, 2262];\n\ncheckRowNums.forEach(rNum => {\n  const r = rows[rNum - 1]; // 1-based index in Excel, rows[0] is header, so rows[rNum - 1] is row rNum\n  if (r) {\n    console.log(`[Row ${rNum}] ${r[2]} | Biz: ${r[3]} | CEO: ${r[6]} | Phone: ${r[7]} | Addr: ${r[10]} | 24s: ${r[16]} | 25s: ${r[17]} | Note: ${r[14]}`);\n  }\n});\n","Description":"Check key rows in master CSV","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a97462f9-3976-4927-b799-281f20134eb3\\scratch\\check_key_rows_in_csv.js","toolAction":"Writing script to check key rows in CSV","toolSummary":"Write check_key_rows_in_csv.js"}}]}
